course: dictionary
lesson: 771
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A beard is the hair that grows on a man's chin and cheeks. But this word has other meanings too, so the context tells you which one the writer means. Look at the words around it before you decide.
explain: «Many goats have beards, both males and females; most sheep do not.» Goats are animals, not men, so here a beard is the hairs on a goat's chin. The clue is the word goats. Ask yourself: does this sentence make sense with my meaning in it?
explain: «Lichen, like old man's beard, is not a plant but a fungus and a tiny green alga living together.» Old man's beard is the name of a kind of lichen, so beard can also be a name for something that is not hair at all.
fact: A beard is the hair that grows on the chin and cheeks of a man.
fact: Some animals, like goats, have beard-like hairs or bristles on their chins.
fact: Some plants, such as barley, have bristles that are also called beards.
fact: Beards grow on men as they become adults.
fact: «Beard» can also be a verb meaning to face someone boldly, but this use is old and rare.
exercise: «Many goats have beards, both males and females; most sheep do not.» What is a goat's beard? | A kind of tail | A type of sheep | *Hairs or bristles on the chin | A horn on the head
exercise: Beards grow on men as they become adults. What is this change called? | Migration | Photosynthesis | Hibernation | *Puberty
exercise: «Hatshepsut sometimes wore a king's false beard.» What does false mean here? | Dirty | *Not real, a fake | Very long | Made of gold
test: «A bearded dragon bobbing its head is signalling that it is in charge.» What is a bearded dragon? | *An animal from the dry lands of Australia | A pirate with a dark beard | A type of lichen | A plant from the desert
test: «Lichen, like old man's beard, is not a plant but a fungus and a tiny green alga living together.» What is lichen? | A kind of sheep | A goat's hair | *A fungus and a tiny green alga living together | A man's chin
exam: Which word means the hair that grows on a man's chin and cheeks? | Barley | Lichen | *Beard | Goat
